WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.819
We did this long form piece in November of
2017 debunking a lot of the myths,

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:08.460
rounding, race and intelligence and Iq.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.019
And we did it right after this topic sort
of exploded with Sam Harris and Charles Murray

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:17.580
and as recline and at the time there was just
a ton of discussion on youtube and elsewhere

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.550
about race and Iq and I thought it was necessary
at the time to deconstruct some of the so

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:27.220
called scientific racism narratives, which
have actually always been around.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.910
But we're really popularized right around
that time, about a year and a half ago or

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:32.910
so.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.479
And I wasn't gonna do any more on the subject.

00:00:34.479 --> 00:00:36.750
I think we said what we needed to say.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:41.109
It's not something that we talk about often
on the program very much anymore, but I decided

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:45.249
to do a sort of one time follow up to that
video.

00:00:45.249 --> 00:00:48.420
Um, based on the feedback that I've gotten
since then.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.670
The video that we originally did got more
than a quarter million views.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:57.030
It has about 30% dislikes, which is not super
surprising.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.359
It still gets views and I'm continuing to
hear from about it.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:05.610
And I want to address a couple of the different
types of criticisms that I get about the video.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:11.580
People have said things like, if it's okay
to say that certain races are better at sports,

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.980
why is it wrong to make the same sort of observations
about race and intelligence?

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:20.750
Now this kind of argument isn't always worded
in this exact same way, but it's a common

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.310
one that you hear.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:27.900
And I think that this athletics and intelligence
analogy could maybe be a good jumping off

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:33.270
point to explore racial taboos and what a
lot of people just aren't understanding about

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.270
this.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:40.800
So to begin with, if we're just talking about
taboos, many people do find it offensive when

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.920
certain races are stereotyped as being better
at sports.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.280
Racial stereotypes tend to be offensive to
a lot of people, whether they're positive

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.050
or negative stereotypes.

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:56.340
But going beyond that, stereotypes about athletic
ability and stereotypes about intellectual

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.880
ability have very different implications.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:03.410
And people who equate the two are just pretending
that they don't know that or genuinely don't

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:04.540
know it.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:10.810
Most employers don't care about the natural
athletic abilities of a job applicant.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:16.810
Being stereotyped as someone who's probably
good at sports or certain sports is not going

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:20.510
to significantly impact you in most of the
real world.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.879
With some exceptions.

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:28.540
Being stereotyped as someone who's probably
smart, very well may help you in life.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:33.849
So being equated, equating athletics with
intelligence in order to argue that race and

00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:40.299
Iq shouldn't be taboo or shouldn't be handled
with sensitivity is probably just pretending

00:02:40.299 --> 00:02:44.480
not to understand that there's a real significant
difference between the two.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:50.049
When someone says, we can talk about race
and athletic ability, so we should be allowed

00:02:50.049 --> 00:02:52.450
to talk about race and intelligence.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:57.889
This person might also be ignoring the social
causes behind why certain races are more successful

00:02:57.889 --> 00:02:59.480
in certain sports.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:05.790
The same way that people ignore the social
aspects of Iq, certain sports are way more

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.219
ingrained in certain cultures.

00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:14.590
So for example, despite Latin Americans, disproportionate
representation in baseball would be pretty

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:20.760
ridiculous to say that they are genetically
predisposed to excel at baseball or to say

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:27.419
that northern Europeans have a genetic inclination
to be better bobsledders.

00:03:27.419 --> 00:03:31.749
In some cultures bowling is more present and
other cultures it's track and field that's

00:03:31.749 --> 00:03:32.840
more common.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:36.980
Basketball plays a bigger role in some cultures
than in others.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:42.370
So someone trying to say that Iq is genetically
tied to race and that we should be allowed

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.419
to talk about it because we do the same thing
for sports might be committing the exact same

00:03:46.419 --> 00:03:52.620
fallacies when thinking about sports as when
they do with Iq from a social perspective

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:58.000
and somebody trying to make this point might
also be failing to recognize that intellectual

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:04.559
ability is orders of magnitude more dynamic
and complex than athletic ability from a biological

00:04:04.559 --> 00:04:07.120
perspective, which they claim to care about.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:13.919
We can say with significant certainty exactly
what makes someone a better runner versus

00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:18.180
being better at lifting heavier weight versus
being better at throwing a ball.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.990
You can't reduce in jet intelligence to the
same kind of analysis.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:27.650
So someone making this argument, comparing
or equating sports to intelligence is on multiple

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:34.540
levels equivocating or not even understanding
this debate in response to what I've previously

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.880
said about race and Iq.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.210
Something else I've been seeing people defend
is this premise that regardless of what other

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:46.120
conclusions we can or cannot make about Iq,
Iq tests are simply really good predictors

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:52.690
of success in life and people often use this
either to justify the utility of Iq tests

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:58.340
and keeping Iq tests as part of the conversation
about race and intelligence as well as to

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:05.510
explain why racist, who score lower on Iq
tests also have lower incomes or whatever

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:08.490
other parameter it is that they're focused
on.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.040
So let's reset this.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:18.510
What Iq tests are best at indicating is whether
or not someone has a serious lack of intelligence.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.510
Okay.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:25.601
Iq tests measure very specific things, short
term memory, some pattern recognition, some

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:32.830
verbal abilities, processing speed to some
degree, visual, spatial processing, a particular

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.520
type of comprehension.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:40.330
There is no question at all that if someone
scores an 80 on an Iq test that they are lacking

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:44.860
in those categories as measured and relevant
by the Iq test.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:48.650
But that's somebody who has some pretty serious
challenges.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:54.670
Anyone who, uh, accepts that Iq tests are
effective at screening out.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:06:00.560
People who have significant cognitive limitations
would then have to ask the question, well,

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:06.820
at minimum if you have normal intelligence
or higher, what is Iq really tell us about

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:07.820
success?

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.470
And the answer is not very much.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:15.120
Iq scores among people with normal intelligence
can give us a sense of who's better at taking

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:21.790
tests or better at accomplishing tasks that
are similar to Iq tests and at doing jobs

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:26.430
that require thinking in narrow boundaries
like an Iq test.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.580
And some might call them paper pushers.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:33.870
That's what an a Taleb calls I why eyes or
intellectuals yet idiots.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.640
This is his term, not mine.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.580
So when we're trying to determine whether
they're actually are correlations between

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.930
Iq and success, how are we measuring success?

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:47.250
Let's for a moment say that you could measure
success by wealth or income.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.680
It's not the only way.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:53.170
Many people do really great important things
and they don't make a lot of money, but in

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:57.580
western capitalist society we might look at
wealth as at least one factor that we would

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:03.490
say success and wealth are not interchangeable
but significantly complimentary.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:10.640
There is no statistically significant correlation
between Iq and wealth beyond seriously cognitively

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.050
limited people.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:17.320
You can definitely come up with some kind
of sort of circular reasoning to say people

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:20.640
with high Iq have more bureaucratic success.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.710
They hold higher positions on paper at different
institutions.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:30.340
They do well in these hierarchically based
jobs that are similar to Iq tests, which wouldn't

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.910
be a big surprise but there's no correlation
with wealth.

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:39.790
When someone with a High Iq has a job with
tasks that are like an Iq test, they're going

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:46.240
to do well, but that doesn't correlate Iq
with success as defined by wealth just with

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.300
success that is similar to the Iq test themselves.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:54.410
Check out this chart plotting net worth versus
Iq at the bottom.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:59.330
You'll see that for Iqs ranging from 70 to
90 there is definitely a clustering of low

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.450
net worth.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:07.080
Once you get past the Iq Range, 70 to 90,
it is a very statistically noisy distribution

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.220
or instead of wealth.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:11.360
You can also look at Iq versus income.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:17.010
Definitely a slight correlation, but income
is not rising nearly as fast as Iq, especially

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:23.820
once you get past that 70 to 90 Iq range where
it almost levels out totally from a scientific

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:24.820
perspective.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:29.720
What we have here is a correlation that works
in the left tail but not the right tail, which

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:36.500
suggests that Iq is mostly useful for identifying
people who are seriously limited in their

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.719
intellectual capacity.

00:08:37.719 --> 00:08:43.650
You see the correlation with so called success
at low Iqs, but the correlation goes away

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:44.760
high iqs.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:49.720
This makes it a bad predictive measure beyond
telling us who has really serious learning

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:54.230
disabilities, which by the way, we can figure
out without Iq tests.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:59.279
Another important factor, uh, you know how
lots of people on the right like to say academia

00:08:59.279 --> 00:09:00.480
isn't real life.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:05.670
They say, you know, the real world simply
doesn't work like an academic sociology department

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.510
or like a liberal arts college.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:11.460
The same applies to the concept of an Iq test.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:16.570
In the real world when you're presented with
Iq type questions, it's not just about getting

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:20.010
the right answer within those artificial constraints.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:22.920
You have to figure out is is this question
relevant?

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:26.880
You have to figure out why am I being asked
this question.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:31.840
You have to figure out is my time better spent
elsewhere than answering this question and

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:38.740
is Nassim Taleb has written an Iq test asks
you in a sequence one, two, three, four x,

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:40.200
what is x?

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:45.640
Finding x in that limited away is very rarely
something people are asked to do in the real

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:51.380
world, but more importantly in the real world
people would say, why is it important to find

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.380
x?

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:59.150
Iq does not measure that, but real world success
depends on that type of thinking.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:06.450
So once again to compare Iq and success, let's
look at Iq relative to specific elements of

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:08.660
job performance.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.529
Correlations go from minus one to one.

00:10:10.529 --> 00:10:15.240
Okay, so anything from zero and up means that
there is a correlation.

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:18.030
A correlation of one would be total correlation.

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:24.260
Like for example, the correlation between
being homo sapiens and being human is one

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.560
training success in the military.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:31.200
And Iq have a slightly larger than 0.6 correlation.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:37.900
On the other hand, job performance in medium
complexity jobs correlates with Iq at about

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.230
0.5.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:46.740
Creativity correlates with Iq below 0.4 and
leader effectiveness correlates with Iq at

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:47.820
roughly 0.3.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:52.720
So you can still look at that and say, well
listen, 0.6 correlations are pretty high and

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:53.850
you're right.

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:59.930
But once you account for a bell curve distribution,
you have to realize why this is a very limited

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:01.510
usefulness to us.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:07.210
If we look at just the correlation between
Iq and performance in general, it looks like

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:08.210
this.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:14.040
This doesn't make any sense unless as I mentioned,
Iq is merely a tool to identify people who

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:19.360
are significantly limited in their intelligence
and cognitive abilities.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:25.130
These correlations are low enough that there
is a massive overlap between supposedly low

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.670
Iq and high Iq jobs.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:31.029
Uh, check out this chart which shows a whole
bunch of different jobs and the Iq ranges

00:11:31.029 --> 00:11:32.530
of the people who do them.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.800
A Quick Lancet at this looks very overwhelming.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:35.800
Wow.

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:41.050
The IQ range of janitors and machine operators
and truck drivers is just so much lower than

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.870
the Iq for doctors and professors and electrical
engineers.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:48.830
But remember these are ranges and if you look
very closely at this, you'll notice that the

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:56.839
top 25% of janitors have a higher Iq than
the bottom 25% of college professors.

00:11:56.839 --> 00:12:02.250
And of course part of this is circular because
medical school requires that you've done well

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:07.770
on things like sats, which correlates with
Iq because they're testing very similar things.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:13.220
Imagine how many lower Iq people could be
doctors if more opportunities were given to

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:18.800
people without high sat scores who might still
be a great doctor or a great professor if

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:25.510
the tests required to be a professor or doctor
require high Iq, that's going to restrict

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:31.240
those fields to people with higher Iq without
ever having to demonstrate that the high Iq

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:34.470
is actually necessary to be successful in
those fields.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:39.220
So yeah, the people who peddle the race realist
stuff about Iq are usually the same people

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:45.140
who have this mantra about how important Iq
is and how fatalistic and linked to success

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:50.380
it is, which makes sense because Iq tests
being relevant or useful to begin with is

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:54.700
a necessary premise for everything else that
follows in these hypotheses.

00:12:54.700 --> 00:13:00.880
They will say Iq tests are an authoritative
measure of intelligence and it's the most

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:06.350
accurate measure of intelligence and of human
potential, and that's how the race realists

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:10.440
ensure that the next claim really comes with
a sting.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:17.560
The claim that black people or Hispanic people
or whoever are on average destined to have

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:18.920
lower iqs.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:24.170
So basically those groups are predetermined
to live measurably lower quality lives and

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:25.170
that's just that.

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:27.740
It might be sad, we might not like it, but
it's the truth.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:32.649
But Iq doesn't measure all types of intelligence
or even measure potential for success in life.

00:13:32.649 --> 00:13:39.190
It doesn't even really measure your full potential
to perform on the IQ tests themselves.

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:45.320
Children's Iq test scores can increase with
certain type of educational interventions

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:51.029
and with changes in environments people have
the same genetic Iq potential for lack of

00:13:51.029 --> 00:13:57.420
a better term, would score differently when
raised in different parental or socioeconomic

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:58.600
situations.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:03.720
Environment is a massive factor and one of
the most interesting counterpoints to the

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:11.580
racial Iq success theory is Polynesians native
Polynesians are a racially or ethnically homogenous

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:17.400
group that's spread out over a massive, massive
environment ranging from within New Zealand,

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:22.080
throughout islands in the Pacific all the
way to Easter island with drastically different

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:27.650
levels of success in economics, in technology
development, in food production, longevity,

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:33.510
and in many other factors what matters, where
the environments they spread to, which allowed

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.850
very different food production.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:40.670
When you have a food production surplus that
dictates when you can actually start to have

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:47.230
members of your population specialize in tasks
beyond the gathering of food itself, you start

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:52.089
to develop politics and technology and ultimately
the level of success as measured by modern

00:14:52.089 --> 00:14:55.380
western standards is heavily dependent on
this.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:59.820
Now, there are ways in which Iq is partly
heritable.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:05.029
There are studies involving identical twins
who are raised in separate environments or

00:15:05.029 --> 00:15:10.150
adopted children not raised by their biological
parents that show this.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:18.140
There is not a total consensus as to to what
degree Iq is heritable or how strong the correlation

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:23.170
is between differences in Iq and differences
in Geno types.

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:28.360
Iq heritability can even vary widely based
on when and where you study it.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:32.040
Under what circumstances making it much more
difficult to nail down.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:37.220
Is it a point to correlation is at 0.5 is
it something else but there's not much disagreement

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:40.320
that Iq can be genetically inherited.

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:44.459
To some extent it's more than zero but it's
definitely not one.

00:15:44.459 --> 00:15:50.990
But then the question is is that the complete
story or even nearly enough of it to what

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:58.200
it tells us about the Iqs of groups of people
and are there other facts that would complicate

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:04.029
things for people who take Quinn's studies
and presume that it points to inherent average

00:16:04.029 --> 00:16:11.010
Iq differences that can be based on race and
the answer is what happens in individuals

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:15.050
does not even necessarily have any bearing
on what happens in groups.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:20.320
Imagine you have group A and Group B group
a has higher average Iq scores Than Group

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:26.550
B and you want to know is that because of
genetic differences between the two groups

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:31.570
to confirm that that's the case, you would
need one specific identifiable genes that

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:37.360
consistently cause people to have higher iqs
and group a would need to on average have

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:40.130
more of those genes than group B has.

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:45.450
And number two, the difference in Iq between
the two groups would need to be greater than

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.900
that which could be explained by the environment.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:52.330
And we know that this isn't the case when
we're talking about races.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:57.980
Research has shown us that the Iq differences
we see between races is no greater than the

00:16:57.980 --> 00:17:03.230
Iq differences we observe between children
raised in different environments.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:09.069
We also know that Iqs in the United States
and worldwide have risen more quickly in the

00:17:09.069 --> 00:17:13.390
past hundred years than could ever be accounted
for by genetics.

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:17.490
Iq is highly malleable depending on environment.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:22.610
And then last but definitely not least as
an extremely important crux in all of this.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:28.650
If you're dealing with something biological,
like genetic Iq, you have to be weighing it

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.160
against something that is also biological.

